ps.push(P("N002","internal","M is stable under X_r,Y_r for every natural r, under x,y,h, and these restrictions satisfy the stated Chevalley bracket relations. iota embeds M_R into V; M_R is free over R of rank n and iota(M_R) complex-linearly spans V. Every X_r,Y_r preserves iota(M_R). For i,j in I, binom(lambda,j) is a unit of R; the operators E_ij preserve iota(M_R) and satisfy E_ij=binom(lambda,j)^(-1) X_(lambda-i) Y_lambda X_lambda Y_(lambda-j). In particular Y_lambda X_lambda=E_(lambda,lambda), X_(lambda-i)E_(lambda,lambda)=E_(i,lambda), and E_(lambda,lambda)Y_(lambda-j)=binom(lambda,j)E_(lambda,j).",["D001","D002","D003","D004","D005","D006","D007","D008","D009","D010"],["M","X","Y","x","y","h","R","M_R","iota","V","n","I","lambda","E"],[B("r","natural number"),B("i","element of I"),B("j","element of I")],"problem.md:86-116; localization and matrix units"));
ps.push(P("N003","internal","All J_i for i in I equal J. J is a nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of C. Under iota, M_R identifies with the internal direct sum of J e_i over i in I; Q tensor_R J has rational dimension one and its multiplication map into C is injective. There exists a complex scalar b!=0 such that b belongs to J, J=R b, and (b e_i)_{i in I} is an R-basis of iota(M_R), equivalently its inverse images form an R-basis of M_R.",["D004","D005","D006","D007","D008","D009","D011","D012"],["J_i","J","I","R","e","iota","M_R"],[B("i","element of I"),B("b","complex number")],"problem.md:118-148; common coordinate module, rank and principality"));
ps.push(P("N004","internal","There exists a K-basis beta=(beta_i)_{i in I} of V_K, so dim_K V_K=n=lambda+1>0. It has generator matrices x_K beta_0=0; x_K beta_i=(lambda-i+1)beta_(i-1) for 1<=i<=lambda; y_K beta_i=(i+1)beta_(i+1) for i<lambda; y_K beta_lambda=0; h_K beta_i=(lambda-2i)beta_i. There are K-linear endomorphisms T_ij of V_K for i,j in I with T_ij beta_k=beta_i if k=j and zero otherwise, and T_ij=binom(lambda,j)^(-1) X_(lambda-i)^K Y_lambda^K X_lambda^K Y_(lambda-j)^K. Here integer coefficients are mapped into K, every binom(lambda,j) is nonzero in K, and X_r^K=(r!)^(-1)x_K^r, Y_r^K=(r!)^(-1)y_K^r for 0<=r<=lambda. The natural K-linear isomorphisms V_K -> M_R tensor_R K -> (M_R/pM_R) tensor_(F_p) K intertwine these induced lattice operators; the first sends m tensor c to (1 tensor m) tensor c and its inverse sends (r tensor m) tensor c to m tensor (bar(r)c), where bar:R->K is the extension of the integer map. The second sends u tensor c to (u mod pM_R) tensor c.",["D001","D002","D004","D005","D007","D008","D013","D014","D015"],["K","p","V_K","n","lambda","I","rho","M_R","R","M","X","Y","L_K"],[B("beta","family of vectors of V_K indexed by I"),B("T_ij","family of K-linear endomorphisms of V_K indexed by I times I"),B("i","element of I"),B("j","element of I"),B("k","element of I"),B("r","element of R or nonnegative divided-power index as specified in the separate clauses"),B("m","element of M"),B("c","element of K"),B("u","element of M_R")],"problem.md:150-170; reduction and scalar extension"));
